// Factions of 3025. Typed against domain/faction.zig `FactionRow`.
// Canonical columns (name, capital, color, foes, hires) adapted from
// MekHQ universe/Faction / factions.xml (ARCH §9.1).
// `pay_bp` is a project-chosen employer multiplier. // TUNE
// `foes` feeds the contract market's enemy picks; `hires` whether the
// faction posts contracts; `color` is the Map screen's political colouring.
//
// Economy columns (docs/p3c-economy-design.md §3):
// `manufacturing_chassis` — chassis keys (data/chassis.zon) this faction
//   manufactures. Provisional stand-in derived from that faction's own RAT
//   heavy+assault pools (data/tables/rat.zon), deduplicated. These are
//   UNVERIFIED manufacturing membership, distinct from RAT fielding; must be
//   re-sourced from force sheets / TechManual before P3e.6 balances on them.
//   PER (pirates / near Periphery), CS (ComStar), and the seven Periphery
//   states with no RAT row have empty lists pending sourcing. // TUNE
// `replenishment_hulls_per_year` — whole battlemechs the faction adds to its
//   own roster per year; 0 for empty-list factions. // TUNE
// `conflict_sensitivity_bp` — basis points (0..=100_000) governing how
//   sharply faction conflict reduces surplus flow to market. // TUNE
